mike/bus/inbox/Winston.jsonl:438:{"event_id": "395d72c6-8154-45f9-a65c-e6b45e1bf3aa", "ts": "[REDACTED]02T08:41:37Z", "agent_id": "Winston", "event_type": "finding", "topic": "quant-skeptic-[REDACTED]D-fix-nav-co-tuc", "payload": {"job": "Winston_20260802_082040", "gate": "quant-skeptic (bin/verify_finding.sh)", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "high", "log": "mike/logs/verify_20260802_083722.log", "reviewer_da_tu_lam_lai": "chay lai nav_cum_dividend_selfcheck.py duoi env -u TZ -> 38/38 PASS y het; tu query BQ lai ti so Close/Price cua BID (0.98855 -> 1.0 ngay 17/07, suy ra 450d/cp) va NCT (0.913793 -> 1.0 ngay 27/07, suy ra 8000d/cp) -> ra dung 5 con so; tu doc dnse_raw_[REDACTED]{15,16}.jsonl thay delta cashDividendReceiving = dung 855.000; doi chieu CSV tren dia voi ban .bak", "killer_objection_con_lai": "che do live dung heuristic thoi diem (ban ghi balance phien truoc >=16:00 = cuoi ngay) chu khong phai ground-truth; ca la (2 su kien co tuc cung 1 toi, hoac balance ve muon ngoai nhip) co the danh bai quy tac nay. Giam nhe bang thiet ke: ca khong ket luan duoc thi FAIL-SAFE canh bao chu khong tu tru (da chung minh bang ca am [REDACTED] 09/07).", "reruns_de_xuat": ["mo rong bo ca selfcheck moi khi co su kien co tuc moi", "sua not [REDACTED] 22/07 sau khi user duyet", "vai tuan nua doi chieu che do live vs rerun tren [REDACTED] that"], "ket_luan": "CA 2 VIEC HOAN TAT, qua gate."}, "kb_version": 1620, "trace_id": "Winston_20260802_082040"}
mike/bus/inbox/quant-skeptic.jsonl:109:{"event_id": "41574280-7e87-4253-b298-3b99175588c0", "ts": "[REDACTED]02T08:40:58Z", "agent_id": "quant-skeptic", "event_type": "verification", "topic": "VERIFY: fix-nav-dem-2-lan-co-tuc-cum-date", "payload": {"finding_topic": "fix-nav-dem-2-lan-co-tuc-cum-date", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "na — this is an accounting/bookkeeping correction (NAV cash reconciliation), not a trading signal/filter; it never touches profit_2W/1M/2M/3M, O1W..O2Y, *_center_*, or Pattern_*_3Y. The 'rerun' mode does read BQ rows dated after the target date to resolve historical ex-dates, but only for retroactive NAV bookkeeping and only when BQ has since caught up — never used to size or time a live trade. The genuinely live path ('live' mode, BQ not yet caught up) correctly falls back to a same-day timing heuristic and fails safe (returns a warning, does not guess) exactly on the one adversarial case built for it ([REDACTED] [REDACTED]09 MBB, already-past ex-date).", "oos_robustness": "na — not a return-generating signal; no IS/OOS split applies to a bookkeeping bug fix.", "panel_curation_bias": "na — not a universe/backtest claim.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — independently re-ran `env -u TZ python3 mike/bin/nav_cum_dividend_selfcheck.py` myself: got exactly 38 PASS / 0 FAIL, matching the claim verbatim, including the adversarial negative case ([REDACTED] [REDACTED]09, dividend already past ex-date -> correctly NOT subtracted) and the rerun/live-mode agreement check.", "param_overfit": "na — no tunable parameter; CUM_DIV_EOD_HHMM='16:00' is a fixed operational cutoff, not a fit parameter, and is exercised correctly by the selfcheck's boundary cases.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — not a capacity-sensitive trading edge; this is NAV bookkeeping for 2 live accounts.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "pass — verified all 5 approved fixes arithmetically: nav_moi = nav_cu - loai and cash_moi = cash_cu - loai hold exactly for all 5 rows (e.g. [REDACTED] 07-16: 957,558,637-855,000=956,703,637 and 305,388,637-855,000=304,533,637), and confirmed these exact post-fix values are what's actually written in [REDACTED]ogs/nav_history_{[REDACTED],[REDACTED]}.csv today (diffed against the .bak_20260802 backups). Re-running fix_nav_cum_dividend_20260802.py now correctly detects the file is already fixed and halts rather than double-applying (idempotency works as designed). Scope-boundary claims verified: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] is confirmed left UNFIXED in the live CSV (886,083,813/21,640,713, matching the 'out of approved scope' note), [REDACTED] has no NAV row on [REDACTED] (confirmed empty), and [REDACTED] [REDACTED] (a day with no corporate action) is unchanged with cum_dividend_excl=0, i.e. no regression on unaffected days.", "independent_recompute": "Cross-checked the two largest ticker events independently via fresh BQ queries: BID Close/Price ratio jumps from 0.98855 ([REDACTED]) to exactly 1.0 ([REDACTED]) -> ex-date [REDACTED], implied dividend/share = 39300*(1-0.98855) ≈ 450đ, matching the claimed 450đ/share for both [REDACTED] (1900cp*450=855,000) and [REDACTED] (900cp*450=405,000) exactly. NCT ratio jumps from 0.913793 ([REDACTED]) to exactly 1.0 ([REDACTED]) -> ex-date [REDACTED], implied dividend/share = 92800*(1-0.913793) ≈ 8000đ, matching [REDACTED] (500cp*8000=4,000,000) and [REDACTED] (373cp*8000=2,984,000) exactly. Also independently read the raw dnse_raw_[REDACTED]{15,16}.jsonl balances for [REDACTED] (account [REDACTED]) and found cashDividendReceiving jumped from 2,400,000 to 3,255,000, a delta of exactly 855,000 -- matching the claimed cash amount to the đồng. Additionally ran mike/bin/nav_scripts_2account_selfcheck.py fresh: reproduced the claimed pre-existing, unrelated FAIL (verify_account_snapshot.py reporting mtm=0.0 for both accounts on a no-fill day) and confirmed daily_nav_snapshot.py itself runs rc=0 live end-to-end for both accounts with no regression."}, "killer_objection": "The fix itself is a one-off hardcoded FIXES dict patching 5 known historical rows; the real safeguard against recurrence is that cum_dividend_double_count() is now wired into daily_nav_snapshot.py's live main() path (confirmed at line 436) so future ex-date events are caught automatically going forward. The one residual soft spot is the 'live' mode's same-day fallback heuristic (prev balance record timestamp >= 16:00 => treat as EOD => subtract) — this is a timing heuristic, not a ground-truth check, and it is only validated against the 12 cases in the selfcheck's fixed test set; a not-yet-seen edge case (e.g. two dividend events landing on the account in the same evening, or a broker balance update arriving late/out of the normal cadence) could in principle defeat the >=16:00 rule. This is mitigated by design: ambiguous cases fail safe with a warning rather than silently subtracting (demonstrated by the [REDACTED] [REDACTED]09 negative case), so a novel edge case would surface as a flagged warning for human review rather than a silent wrong NAV.", "recommended_reruns": ["Re-run nav_cum_dividend_selfcheck.py periodically as new dividend events land on [REDACTED]/[REDACTED] to keep expanding the adversarial case list beyond the current 12 hand-picked cases.", "Follow up on the disclosed-but-unapproved [REDACTED] [REDACTED] (+832,500đ CTG/VCB) double-count once the user reviews and approves it, using the same script/pattern.", "After a few more weeks of live 19:10 same-day runs, spot-check that the 'live' mode fallback (>=16:00 heuristic) never disagreed with the next day's BQ-confirmed 'rerun' mode in [REDACTED] (not just in the synthetic selfcheck cases)."], "summary": "This is a real, well-diagnosed bug fix, not a mirage: DNSE records a cash dividend receivable into totalCash on the last cum-date evening while the closing price that same session still includes the dividend (cum), so summing stock(cum price) + cash(incl. receivable) double-counts the dividend for exactly one session, self-cancelling the next day when the price goes ex-div — which is precisely why every prior NAV reconciliation passed and the bug survived undetected. I independently reproduced the mechanism and every headline number: re-ran the cited selfcheck myself under env -u TZ and got the exact same 38/38 PASS (including its key adversarial negative case), independently queried BigQuery for BID and NCT Close/Price ratios and derived the same ex-dates and per-share dividend amounts (450đ and 8000đ respectively) that produce the exact five corrected NAV/cash deltas, independently read the raw DNSE balance JSONL and found the same 855,000đ cashDividendReceiving delta for [REDACTED]'s BID case, and confirmed the actual nav_history CSVs on disk already reflect the corrected values (matching the .bak backups' pre-fix state exactly). The fix correctly stopped at the 5 user-approved rows, correctly declined to touch a 6th known-affected but unapproved row ([REDACTED] [REDACTED], documented transparently for separate approval), correctly identified a day with no NAV row to fix ([REDACTED] [REDACTED]), and left an unrelated day ([REDACTED] 07-31) untouched with zero regression. The fix logic is also wired into the live [REDACTED] path (daily_nav_snapshot.py main(), not just the selfcheck), so it will catch future occurrences automatically rather than being a pure backfill patch. None of the look-ahead/OOS/panel-curation/capacity attacks apply since this is not a trading signal. I found no defect that survives scrutiny."}, "kb_version": 1619, "trace_id": "Winston_20260802_082040"}

